{"step_index":286,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T19:24:36Z","thinking":"**Addressing Aggressive CSS Caching**\n\nThe primary concern involves browser caching of static resources like the CSS file, potentially leading to users seeing outdated styles. Updating the external stylesheet alone may not be sufficient.\n\nThe strategy involves two actions: updating the external `style.css` file and including an embedded `<style>` block directly within the `login.html` file. This combination will ensure the most recent CSS definitions are always rendered, as the embedded styles have the highest precedence.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Styling Details**\n\nThe `login.html` styling is broken down into four key sections: background, navbar, authentication card, and header, each requiring specific CSS attributes. Background utilizes a radial gradient and decorative patterns for visual appeal. The navbar employs glassmorphism with a logo and links; the logo is a gradient square with text, and links require hover effects.\n\nThe authentication card, centered with rounded borders, will have a box shadow, padding, and a white background. The header incorporates a circular badge with a gradient, border, shadow, and centered text for authentication details.\n\n\n**Defining Form Input Styles**\n\nForm groups will have bottom margins and a vertical layout with left text alignment. Labels are flex containers, space-between aligned with font size, weight, color, and margin. Input elements use absolute positioning for icons and actions.\n\nInput controls are styled with specific dimensions, background, border, border-radius, padding, font properties, and outline, ensuring a consistent visual appearance. Right-side actions use transparent backgrounds, rounded borders, padding, a pointer cursor, and color transitions.\n\n\n**Defining Form Component Styles**\n\nThe input field styling includes a subtle shadow, smooth transitions, and distinct hover/focus states, ensuring visual feedback.  Password inputs receive specific padding to accommodate icons and actions.\n\nThe submit button will have a gradient background, white text, and rounded corners, along with a prominent shadow effect. It also incorporates transitions for hover and active states, providing dynamic feedback to the user.\n\n**Constructing Demo Account Display**\n\nThe demo account section's format should be a grid or responsive card list, displaying quick demo accounts. Each account card will include an icon, role description, and credentials, promoting a user-friendly way to access demonstration data. The header should contain a title and badge, indicating auto-fill functionality.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\">\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\">\\n    <title>Authorized Portal Authentication | DevOps QVS</title>\\n    <link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\\\">\\n    <link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\\\" crossorigin>\\n    <link href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\">\\n    <link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"/css/style.css?v=sky4\\\">\\n    <style>\\n        /* Scoped High-Impact Presentation Styles for Auth Portal */\\n        body {\\n            background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% -20%, #dbeafe 0%, #eff6ff 25%, #f8fafc 65%, #f1f5f9 100%);\\n            min-height: 100vh;\\n            display: flex;\\n            flex-direction: column;\\n            font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\\n            margin: 0;\\n            color: #0f172a;\\n        }\\n\\n        .auth-nav {\\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);\\n  