{"step_index":288,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T19:25:07Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. now lets add deatils into our databse using the names of ZIMBABWE STATE UNIVERSITY DEGREES ALSO .. AT LIST 10 STUDENTS PER EACH USINVESITY AND HAVING DIFFRENT DEGREES .AS FOR ZOU USE THIS FORMAT DEGREES IN IT ITM 190020 ETC .. AND FOR PGDE USE THIS FORMAT EH250001  WHER THE FIRST 2 DIGIT SHOULD BE A YEAR .  SO UR DATABSE SHOULD HAVE AT 70 AND ABOVE DATA . . \n2.   the css is not good make the textboxes and form be presenatable \n3. style that page such it will be more presentatable \n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Requests**:\n  1. Populate database with Zimbabwe State University degrees, at least 10 students per university with different degrees.\n     - For ZOU: IT degrees format `ITM 190020`, PGDE format `EH250001` (where first 2 digits are the year). Total records: 70+ in database.\n  2. UI/CSS Overhaul: Fix unpresentable, clunky textboxes and forms on the authentication and credential verification pages (specifically `login.html`, `#verificationInput`, `#qualificationForm`).\n- **Success Criteria**:\n  - 83 qualifications seeded across 8 Zimbabwe State Universities + 2 baseline institutions, all notarized on the blockchain.\n  - Verification lookups succeed by Student ID (e.g. `ITM 190020`, `EH250001`) as well as Certificate Number and SHA-256 fingerprint.\n  - Presentable, modern, responsive form and textbox styling matching professional fintech/SaaS portals (full-width textboxes, clean white background, SVG icons, password visibility toggle, elegant demo matrix).\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Database & Backend**:\n  - `src/main/java/com/devops/qvs/config/DataInitializer.java`: Seeded 8 Zimbabwe State Universities (UZ, NUST, MSU, ZOU, CUT, BUSE, GZU, HIT) with 10 distinct students & degrees each (80 r\n<truncated 2683 bytes>\nsure instant rendering regardless of caching.\n- **Write Tool Constraint**: `ArtifactMetadata` must NOT be passed to `write_to_file` when modifying project files outside the `brain/` directory.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- Workspace: `C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\qualification-verification-system`\n- Application startup script: `.\\run-app.bat` (launches Spring Boot server on port 8080).\n- Credentials for testing:\n  - Admin: `admin` / `Admin@12345`\n  - ZOU Officer: `officer_zou` / `Officer@12345`\n  - NIT Officer: `officer` / `Officer@12345`\n  - Verifier: `verifier` / `Verifier@12345`\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. Sync Maven compiled classes/resources by running `mvn process-resources` or `mvn test-compile` if not already synced to `target/classes`.\n2. Proactively launch or confirm running server if requested using `run-app.bat` or `mvn spring-boot:run`.\n3. Respond to user feedback on the updated `login.html` layout and verify if any further dashboard/public portal pages require visual adjustments.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 5 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1789237798105]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2521cc9f-1824-4718-8f41-13ddedc3e34e/.user_uploaded/media_1789237798105.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-12T18:30:27Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1789238251713]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2521cc9f-1824-4718-8f41-13ddedc3e34e/.user_uploaded/media_1789238251713.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-12T18:37:32Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1789238411023]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2521cc9f-1824-4718-8f41-13ddedc3e34e/.user_uploaded/media_1789238411023.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-12T18:40:11Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///